2. Secret-detection rules, in lib/reminisce/secret_guard.ex

   The patterns of these rules are derived from the default configuration of
   gitleaks 8.28.0 (config/gitleaks.toml): private_key (its header),
   aws_access_key, gcp_api_key, azure_ad_client_secret, github_token,
   github_fine_grained_pat, gitlab_token, slack_token, slack_webhook,
   stripe_key, square_token, jwt, npm_token, pypi_token, anthropic_key,
   openai_key, digitalocean_token, shopify_token, hashicorp_vault_token,
   sendgrid_key (sendgrid-api-token) and twilio_key; the key words of
   generic_assignment follow gitleaks' generic-api-key. They were shortened, bounded and in places merged or
   widened here. gcp_service_account and url_credentials are not gitleaks'
   rules.

   Source: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks. Licence: MIT.

